{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",

  // Managed sessions run on a hosted model. Local models stay available as an explicit
  // per-session opt-in — N concurrent sessions against one local Ollama serialize.
  //
  // Hosted concurrency is TESTED, not assumed: 4 sessions fired simultaneously at one
  // `opencode serve` completed in 5.72s wall — exactly the slowest single turn — against
  // 10.45s run serially. The server does not serialize. Per-turn latency does degrade under
  // load (2.4-2.7s solo -> 2.8-5.7s at 4-way), so expect ~1.8x throughput at N=4, not 4x.
  // Also TESTED: a session parked on permission.asked does NOT stall the others — three
  // concurrent sessions finished while the blocked one hung (and it hangs forever; there is
  // no timeout on a pending permission).
  //
  // gpt-5.6-sol limits: context 1,050,000 / limit.input 922,000 / output 128,000.
  "model": "openai/gpt-5.6-sol",
  "small_model": "openai/gpt-5.6-sol",

  // Compaction OFF is a QUALITY decision, not a cost one, and it is the right call:
  // handing a fresh session a passover prompt beats compacting, because compaction loses
  // specificity while re-discovery costs only a little bloat. Retirement is therefore the
  // sole lifecycle policy and auto-compaction must not silently extend a session past it.
  //
  // Set HERE and not via OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOCOMPACT: the env var only reaches the legacy
  // compactor (config.ts:579), while this key is read by both. See docs/SCAN.md C2.
  //
  // CONSEQUENCE, and it is not documented upstream: with auto:false, overflow.ts:28
  // (`if (input.cfg.compaction?.auto === false) return false`) disables the overflow check
  // entirely, and processor.ts:607-613 turns a real context overflow into
  // finish:"error" + status idle. So the ceiling is a HARD ERROR, not a compaction.
  //
  // THE CEILING IS ~360K, NOT 922,000. This comment used to read "with a 922,000-token input
  // limit and a 350K retirement threshold there is ~570K of headroom, so this is a safety net
  // rather than a path anything should reach". MEASURED in Phase 5, and it is false: a session
  // driven up at the then-default 350K took its last successful turn at occupancy 359,829 and
  // then failed 25 CONSECUTIVE turns with the provider's ContextOverflowError. The registry's
  // 922,000 does not describe this provider path. The retirement default came down to 256,000
  // as a result, with a hard gate at 330,000. See docs/HARDEN.md §6 and docs/HEADLESS.md.
  //
  // The control terminal must still render that error state, because to the grid a hard
  // overflow looks like an ordinary idle-after-error.
  "compaction": {
    "auto": false
  },

  // trim-tools: trims generic prose out of tool descriptions via the tool.definition hook.
  // OFF by default — set HARNESS_TRIM_TOOLS=1 to enable. See docs/STRIP.md.
  //
  // healbot: two halves sharing one implementation of retirement. (a) HEADLESS automatic
  // retirement — the guard that keeps a session from reaching the ceiling above. It lives here
  // rather than in the TUI because a fleet left running with no client attached must still
  // retire; server plugins load in `opencode serve` AND in the server the TUI hosts in-process,
  // so one registration covers both topologies. Kill switch: HEALBOT_AUTO_RETIRE=0. (b) the
  // control agent's tools. See docs/HEADLESS.md.
  "plugin": ["./plugin/trim-tools.ts", "./plugin/healbot.ts"],

  // The control agent's tools are DENIED globally and allowed back in agent/control.md.
  //
  // This is about standing token cost, which is what this whole harness exists to cut. Tool
  // definitions are the largest single block of context — 11 shipped tools measure 19,898 B —
  // and five more would be rent every session pays forever for a capability only one agent uses.
  //
  // The mechanism is specific and easy to get wrong: `Permission.disabled`
  // (permission/index.ts:204-215) removes a tool from the request payload only when the LAST
  // rule matching it has `pattern: "*"` and `action: "deny"`. A string value here expands to
  // exactly that (`:190`). The agent's own permission block is merged last (agent/agent.ts:293),
  // so control.md's `allow` wins the findLast and the tools exist for it alone. A SCOPED deny
  // would leave the definitions in every prompt and only block execution — all of the cost, none
  // of the benefit.
  "permission": {
    "healbot_*": "deny"
  }
}
